                "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
                "markdown": "![Daily Aleph Bet: Mem Sofit | Shlomo&#39;s Drash](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/10110529-2762-0139-0000-48682c57e66d:20)\n![Mem Sofit Flashcard — Akhlah](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/10110529-2762-0139-0000-48682c57e66d:21)\n![Hebrew for Kids: The Letter MEM (19) – MazorBooks](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/10110529-2762-0139-0000-48682c57e66d:22)\n![Mem Sofit Stock Illustrations – 14 Mem Sofit Stock ...](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/10110529-2762-0139-0000-48682c57e66d:23)\n![Hebrew Font. the Hebrew Language. the Letter Mem Sofit ...](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/10110529-2762-0139-0000-48682c57e66d:24)\n\nThe [Hebrew Letter Mem](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mem) is the `thirteenth letter of the Hebrew alphabet` , with the sound \"m\" and a numerical value of **40**.[[1]](https://hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Mem/mem.html)[[2]](https://mazorbooks.wordpress.com/2021/05/25/mem/)\n\n### Forms\n\n- **Medial/Initial Mem (מ):** Used at the start or in the middle of a word; open at the bottom-left corner.[[1]](https://his-israel.com/the-hebrew-letter-mem-tishrei/)\n- **Mem Sofit (ם):** The final form used exclusively at the end of a word; it forms a closed square shape.[[1]](https://hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Mem/mem.html)[[2]](https://mazorbooks.wordpress.com/2021/05/25/mem/)[[3]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4Y3FRJe6Xzo&t=4)\n\n### Symbolic Meanings\n\n- **Water (*Mayim*):** It represents flowing water, wisdom, and the Torah.[[1]](https://hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Mem/mem.html)[[2]](https://www.facebook.com/groups/1687050108451278/posts/2045457555943863/)\n- **Revealed vs. Concealed:** The open medial Mem symbolizes revealed truth, while the closed Mem Sofit represents hidden or secret truths, the womb (*rechem* ), or the closed era of the Messiah.[[1]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137085/jewish/Mem.htm)[[2]](https://hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Mem/mem.html)\n- **The Number 40:** Symbolizes periods of testing, transformation, or completion—such as the 40 days of rain in the flood, 40 years of desert wandering, and Moses staying on Mount Sinai for 40 days.[[1]](https://hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Mem/mem.html)[[2]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137085/jewish/Mem.htm)\n\nWould you like to explore **gematria calculations** for words starting or ending with Mem Sofit, or learn how to write it in Hebrew script?",
